-- A `view` whose body, past its `let`s, calls a helper for its markup is
-- neither markup written in place nor an `if` or a `case`, which
-- `browser-direct` compiles as a `view`'s body (docs/design/browser-direct.md
-- §5.5, §11.1; S4's amendment, as amended by its review): `not_implemented`
-- at the field, naming `<>{…}</>`, where §9.2 writes the helper in place.
import Html exposing (Html)
import Tea


page : Bool → Html {}
page on = <b>{if on then "on" else "off"}</b>


view : Bool → Html {}
view on =
    shown = not on

    page shown


main : Tea.Program
main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → True, update = λ_ m → m, view = view }
